WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.769
-GOP Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:05.371
falsely cited HIPAA

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:07.607
in refusing to say whether
she's been vaccinated,

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.143
while Republicans fought
with an ice cream company

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.411
and said we should just learn
to live with climate change.

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:14.714
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:18.618
♪♪

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.586
There's a lot going on
in the world right now

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.855
and it's easy to look around
at the state of things

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.790
and get a slightly
apocalyptic vibe.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.160
COVID cases have
nearly tripled in two weeks,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.562
thanks to a highly
contagious new variant;

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.531
billionaires are
jetting off to space

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.199
as U.S. life expectancy

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:35.467
saw its biggest drop
since World War II;

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.570
and, thanks to intense wildfires
on the West Coast,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.138
smoke blanketed parts
of the country

00:00:39.138 --> 00:00:40.507
as far east as New York.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.275 line:0%
-Dozens of Western wildfires

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.443 line:0%
burning out of control,

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.178 line:0%
sending smoke as far east
as New York City.

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:47.981 line:0%
Nearly 3,000 miles away,

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:51.216 line:0%
air quality in the Northeast,
including here in New York City,

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:54.721 line:0%
was compromised, due to smoke
from those wildfires.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.889 line:0%
-The smoky infernos out west

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:59.793 line:0%
creating hazy skies thousands
of miles away,

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.161 line:0%
stretching from Toronto
to Philadelphia.

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.730 line:0%
The wildfires so strong
in New York City,

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:07.300 line:0%
a plume of haze clouded
the city skyline.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.968 line:0%
-I mean, this is
pretty thick stuff.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.503 line:0%
I mean, it was just draped

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.471 line:0%
across the Statue of Liberty.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:14.941
-Oh, my God!
I mean, on a good day,

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.709
breathing the air
in New York City

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:20.246
is like smoking Marlboro reds
in a railroad cattle car.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.048
[ Laughter ]
You know how bad it has to be

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.649
to notice the air quality
in New York?

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:26.619
That's like noticing a ketchup
stain on a red couch.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:29.489
[ Laughter ]
A thick plume of smoke
turning the sun red

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.090
and blanketing
the Statue of Liberty?

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.626
It's like the establishing shot
in a sci-fi movie

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.495
that takes place
in a dystopian future,

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.630
after a nuclear war
between humans and lizards.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.198
And I want to be
the recluse scientist

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:40.199
with a long, gray beard

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:41.333
who's been living
on the top floor

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:42.668
of the abandoned
Empire State Building.

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:44.870
And then, the last
surviving humans come to me

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:46.672
and they ask
about the formula I devised

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:47.940
for filtering ash
from the sky,

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.375
which would allow the Sun
to break through

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.609
and kill the lizards
because they're

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.311
from a different galaxy.
Our Sun is lethal to them.

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.847
But I get upset because they're
dredging up painful memories.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.115
"Damn you for coming here!"
I'll say.

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.349
"Now, leave me in peace!"

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:59.151
While I clutch a framed photo
of my late wife

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.986
and listen to my Beatles LPs
and they'll say,

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:02.355
"Please, is there anything
we can do for you

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.389
that might change your mind?"

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.824
And I'll pause and I'll say,
"Well,

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.058
I've never seen Hamilton,"
and they'll say,

00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:07.059
"It's still sold out."

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:08.494
And I'll say, "Still?!

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:09.495
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:12.265
Damn you, Lin-Manuel Miranda!"

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.500
Anyway, if you're intrigued
by any of that little teaser,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.902
you can read
the rest right here,

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.536
in my 600-page screenplay,
called

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:18.971 line:0%
"Red Sun's Out,
Space Guns Out."

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.940
[ Laughter ]
Now,

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.808
[Thud]
probably, due in part

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:24.276
to the post-apocalyptic scenes

00:02:24.276 --> 00:02:26.846 line:0%
of mass animal extinctions,
deadly heat waves,

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.848 line:0%
flooded subway stations
in New York City,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.584 line:0%
smoke blanketing the sky
and turning the Sun blood-red,

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:34.720 line:0%
and rings of fire
in the Gulf of Mexico,

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.623
Americans now list
climate change

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.391
as their second-highest priority

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.827
in at least one poll conducted
by The Economist and YouGov.

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.529
But if you're worried
about it, good news --

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:46.699
Fox News host Jesse Waters
has a solution --

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:47.901
just live with it.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.868 line:0%
-If you want to stop
climate change,

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:51.871 line:0%
you don't fight climate change.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.906 line:0%
If it's getting warmer,
you adapt to it.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:56.442 line:0%
Let's just say
the sea levels rise

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.979 line:0%
a couple inches over the
next century, Harold.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.249 line:0%
Okay. It's a great
civilization we have here.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.051 line:0%
I think we can adapt to that.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:08.187 line:0%
The Netherlands --
25% below sea level.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.123 line:0%
They're like a powerhouse
in Europe.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.124 line:0%
-They didn't just destroy
their economy

00:03:12.124 --> 00:03:14.594 line:0%
to fight the rise
in the sea levels right there.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:17.496 line:0%
They built reservoirs
and kind of adjusted

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.465 line:0%
around the coastline
and they're fine.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.901 line:0%
They didn't have
to break the bank to do it.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.303
-Yeah, just adapt to it.

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:26.839
Who needs a cab,
when you could Uber a dolphin?

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.374
Of course, the problem
with Uber dolphins is

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.075
they can't take a hint
when you don't want to talk.

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:31.443
[ High-pitched ]
"So, you from around here?"

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:32.612
[ Laughter ]
Uh, yeah.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.013
"Got plans for the weekend?"

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:36.015
Um, what?
Sorry, I'm kind of busy.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.049
"Oh, okay.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:39.118
Hey, you know,
I could get some krill?"

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.353
Uh, nice try,

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:44.423
but you don't eat krill,
Dolphin.

00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:46.626
Baleen whales do.
You eat small fish.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:47.694
If you want to get
into "Corrections,"

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:48.861
you got to try harder than that.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:49.862
Wait.
This is my stop.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:53.398
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.398 --> 00:03:54.534
Miami's bracing for...

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.439
What's Pitbull supposed to do,
move to Kansas?

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.408
I don't think gasoline is going
to go over too well

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.243
at the Leavenworth County Fair.

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:06.545
Also, your Netherlands
comparison only makes sense

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:09.282
if sea levels stay exactly where
they are right now forever,

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.783
which is obviously
not happening.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.652
That's why the government
is aiming...

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.423
Those changes are necessary

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.759
to avoid potentially
catastrophic flooding

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.527
that could sink low-lying areas.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.177
Experts are
quite literally afraid

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.446
parts of the country
could become uninhabitable.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.925
As one Dutch professor
of geosciences

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.627
and physical geography
put it...

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:11.110
And, when a Dutch professor
uses the expression,

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.880
"[bleep] hits the fan,"
you know the problem is real.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.280
And, you know,
I used to live in Amsterdam

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:16.849
and I called a Dutch friend
and I asked her,

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.184
"How would a Dutch person say,
'The [bleep] hits the fan?'"

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:21.120
And she said, "We would say,
'The [bleep] hits the fan,"

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.355
because we all speak English
and it's an American expression.

00:05:23.355 --> 00:05:24.389
And I said, "Yeah, yeah, yeah,

00:05:24.389 --> 00:05:25.458
but how would you say it
in Dutch?"

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:26.558
And she said,
"I don't want to do this.

00:05:26.558 --> 00:05:27.860
This is a waste of time."

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.194
And I said, "Come on,
just do it. It'll be funny."

00:05:29.194 --> 00:05:30.763
How would you say, 'The [bleep]
hits the fan' in Dutch?"

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.231
And she took a long beat
and said,

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:35.201
"De poep in de ventilator."

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.636
[ Laughter ]
And I said, "And no one's time

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:39.438
has been wasted today."

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:40.840
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.875
So life expectancy
is plummeting,

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.610
a new variant
of a highly contagious

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.345
respiratory disease is surging,

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:49.082
and wildfire smoke has spread
all the way around the U.S.

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:51.417
Let's check in
on Republican politicians

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.518
and see what they're up to.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.086 line:0%
-Senator James Lankford

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.588 line:0%
now calling on the state
of Oklahoma

00:05:56.588 --> 00:05:57.890 line:0%
to ban the sale

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.392 line:0%
of Ben &amp; Jerry's ice cream.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:01.027 line:0%
All of this came
after Ben &amp; Jerry's

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:02.928 line:0%
releasing a statement
earlier this week

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.097 line:0%
saying that they will end
the sale of their ice cream

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:08.000 line:0%
"in the Occupied Palestinian
territory."

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.603 line:0%
Senator Lankford tweeting out
within the hour, saying...

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:26.352 line:0%
...We should immediately block
the sale of all #Benandjerrys

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:28.721 line:0%
in the state
and any state-operated facility

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.756 line:0%
to align with our law."

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:32.091
-Cool, they're fighting
with ice cream, now.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.527
What's next, they going
to accuse Mayor McCheese

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.028
of voting twice in Arizona?

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.763
You can't just ban Ben &amp; Jerry's

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:39.231
because you don't like
their opinions.

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:41.868
I mean, I still eat it,
even though I'm annoyed

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.469
they haven't given us
our own flavor yet.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:44.904
It would be called
A Closer Lick

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:47.172
and we've already mocked up what
the container would look like.

00:06:47.172 --> 00:06:49.008
I sent this to them
and I've called their offices

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:51.210
and left dozens of messages
and all that happened

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:53.045
was one of their interns
called me and said,

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.013
"We already have a flavor
named after you.

00:06:55.013 --> 00:06:56.149
It's called vanilla."

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:57.250
Ha ha ha.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.953
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.588
But I assure you,
if this doesn't work,

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.523
then we will continue
to at least try

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:07.092
to get our own butter flavor,
called Land O' Looks.

00:07:07.092 --> 00:07:10.863
[ Laughter ]
I will have a personalized
dairy product!

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.198
[ Laughter ]
So Republicans think
they should have the power

00:07:13.198 --> 00:07:15.734
to ban an ice cream company,
if they don't like its politics,

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.837
but when President Biden
announced a targeted

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:20.806
community outreach effort
to send volunteers door to door

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:22.642
and raise awareness
about COVID vaccines,

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:24.510
conservatives called it tyranny.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:27.046 line:0%
-And, now, they're starting
to talk about going door to door

00:07:27.046 --> 00:07:28.647 line:0%
to be able to take vaccines

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:30.015 line:0%
to the people.

00:07:30.015 --> 00:07:31.383 line:0%
Think about the mechanisms
they would have to build

00:07:31.383 --> 00:07:34.119 line:0%
to be able to actually execute
that massive of a thing

00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:36.555 line:0%
and then think about what those
mechanisms could be used for.

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:38.324 line:0%
They could then go door to door,
take your guns,

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.393 line:0%
They could then go
door to door, take your Bible.

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:44.230 line:0%
-Marjorie Taylor Greene
tweeting this --

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:47.600 line:0%
"Biden pushing a vaccine
that is NOT FDA approved...

00:07:59.344 --> 00:08:00.479 line:0%
-Going door to door?

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:01.780 line:0%
This is creepy stuff.

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.750 line:0%
You know, someone comes
up to your door outside,

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.351 line:0%
wearing a mask,

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:07.987 line:0%
showing up at your house,

00:08:07.987 --> 00:08:09.889 line:0%
claiming to work
for the government,

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.057 line:0%
asking you personal
medical questions?

00:08:12.057 --> 00:08:15.761 line:0%
-Don't come knocking on my door
with your Fauci Ouchie.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:18.130
-Maybe she thinks that's
a Ben &amp; Jerry's flavor.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.464
I wouldn't be surprised.

00:08:19.464 --> 00:08:21.367
Everyone gets one, but me.

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:23.101
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.101 --> 00:08:26.038
Also, no one's knocking
on your door with a COVID shot,

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:27.639
although I wish they had.
I mean, sure,

00:08:27.639 --> 00:08:29.275
now, certain places,
like New York City,

00:08:29.275 --> 00:08:31.878
will bring the vaccine to your
house, if you sign up for it,

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:34.246
but, back when the rest of us
got ours, a few months ago,

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:36.615
we had to sit at our computers
all day for weeks,

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:38.150
refreshing eight
different websites,

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.987
looking for a random open slot
at a pharmacy at 3:00 am

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:42.822
in a neighborhood
we'd never heard of before.

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:44.823
Honey, I got one.
It's a pharmacy called

00:08:44.823 --> 00:08:47.192
Drugs Plus
in Upper Coney Island West?

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:49.828
I guess I have to take
the George Kennedy Bridge

00:08:49.828 --> 00:08:51.697
to get there?
Is this real?

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:55.667
No polls, Shoemaker,
on the George Kennedy Bridge.

00:08:55.667 --> 00:08:58.471
You just have to eat
50 hard boiled eggs in an hour.

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:00.339
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:02.475
[ As Dragline ]
You can do it, Shoemaker!

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:04.843
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:06.378 line:0%
So, according to Republicans,
they should be able

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:08.180 line:0%
to ban an ice cream company
they don't like,

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.748 line:0%
but going door to door
to raise awareness

00:09:09.748 --> 00:09:11.684 line:0%
about life-saving vaccines
is tyranny.

00:09:11.684 --> 00:09:14.152 line:0%
On Tuesday,
Georgia Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:09:14.152 --> 00:09:17.422 line:0%
was asked by a reporter if she
had personally been vaccinated,

00:09:17.422 --> 00:09:18.958 line:0%
given that she continues to lie

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:21.394 line:0%
and spread dangerous
misinformation
about COVID vaccines.

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.496 line:0%
-Whip Scalise said
that he got vaccinated,

00:09:23.496 --> 00:09:25.598 line:0%
citing this Delta variant
that's going around,

00:09:25.598 --> 00:09:26.732 line:0%
and said he's confident that

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:28.367 line:0%
it's safe and effective.

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.603 line:0%
Two questions. Have you
yourself gotten vaccinated

00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:32.672 line:0%
and do you disagree
with the Republican whip?

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:36.409 line:0%
-Well, your first question
is a violation of HIPAA rights.

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:38.077 line:0%
You see, with HIPAA rights,

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.246 line:0%
we don't have to reveal
our medical records

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.781 line:0%
and that also involves
our vaccine records.

00:09:42.781 --> 00:09:43.982
-That's not a thing.

00:09:43.982 --> 00:09:45.551
A reporter asking you
if you've been vaccinated

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:47.153
doesn't violate
your HIPAA rights,

00:09:47.153 --> 00:09:49.021
any more than a neighbor
needs a warrant

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:50.456
to enter your house
for a barbecue.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:52.024
HIPAA establishes
national standards

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:53.392
to protect your medical records.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:55.160
It doesn't stop journalists
from asking you questions.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:57.463
She probably also thinks
Miranda rights means

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:59.731
she doesn't have to visit her
friends in Manhattan anymore

00:09:59.731 --> 00:10:01.534
after she moves to Brooklyn
with Steve.

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:02.935
[ As Steve ]
Should we just stay in tonight

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:04.103
and watch a movie?

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:06.939
Steve was my audition
for Impression Camp.

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:08.641
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:10.943
They said, "Do one where
we won't know if it's good."

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:12.945
[ Laughter ]
I doubt she even knows

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.346
what HIPAA is
or what it stands for.

00:10:14.346 --> 00:10:16.182
She probably doesn't even know
it's an acronym.

00:10:16.182 --> 00:10:17.916
[ As Greene ] Asking me
if I've been vaccinated

00:10:17.916 --> 00:10:19.318
violates my HIPAA rights

00:10:19.318 --> 00:10:21.053
and asking me
if I've been to the zoo

00:10:21.053 --> 00:10:22.420
violates my hippo rights

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:25.223
and asking me if any
of my siblings are royalty

00:10:25.223 --> 00:10:27.192
violates my Pippa rights.

00:10:27.192 --> 00:10:29.795
[ Laughter ]
And then,

00:10:29.795 --> 00:10:32.831 line:0%
today Texas Congressman
Randy Jackson jumped in

00:10:32.831 --> 00:10:35.234 line:0%
with what he apparently thought
was a brilliant comeback

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:38.270 line:0%
to reporters asking Republicans
if they've been vaccinated.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:39.838 line:0%
-Yeah, I was just going
to chime in and say,

00:10:39.838 --> 00:10:41.139 line:0%
I think that you, as a press,

00:10:41.139 --> 00:10:42.941 line:0%
have a responsibility
to ask questions

00:10:42.941 --> 00:10:44.309 line:0%
of the Democrats as well.

00:10:44.309 --> 00:10:45.744 line:0%
How many of the Democrats
are willing to say

00:10:45.744 --> 00:10:47.512 line:0%
whether or not
they've been vaccinated?

00:10:47.512 --> 00:10:48.814
-Hey, remember that guy,
Dr. Ronny,

00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:51.650
the guy who said Trump had
the IQ of a chess wizard

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.185
and the build
of a college linebacker?

00:10:53.185 --> 00:10:56.155
You know, the guy who was
allegedly known as the Candyman

00:10:56.155 --> 00:10:58.958
because he dished out pills
like the Phoenix Suns gorilla

00:10:58.958 --> 00:11:00.592
giving out T-shirts
at a home game.

00:11:00.592 --> 00:11:02.661
Whenever he handed out
a prescription, this played --

00:11:02.661 --> 00:11:07.800
[ 2 Unlimited's
""Get Ready for This" plays ]

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:11.737
[ Laughter ]

00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:13.672
I'm sure you at least remember
the name Dr. Ronny,

00:11:13.672 --> 00:11:15.674
a name that sounds less like
an actual medical doctor

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:18.411
and more like a guy who plays
jazz, flute, and a fedora

00:11:18.411 --> 00:11:20.045
and invites you
to get sky high with him

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:21.613
in his yurt outside Reno.

00:11:21.613 --> 00:11:22.914 line:0%
Anyway, what are you
talking about?

00:11:22.914 --> 00:11:24.717 line:0%
You don't think Democrats
are willing to say

00:11:24.717 --> 00:11:25.851 line:0%
if they've been vaccinated?

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.353
I'm pretty sure they all
walk around

00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:29.955
with their CDC card Scotch taped
to their foreheads.

00:11:29.955 --> 00:11:31.423
I mean, what else are we going
to do with that thing?

00:11:31.423 --> 00:11:33.692
I thought I was going to have
to show it everywhere I went,

00:11:33.692 --> 00:11:36.795
like a reporter flashing
a press badge at a crime scene,

00:11:36.795 --> 00:11:38.330
and, now, I'm thinking
of taking it out of my wallet

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.698
to make room
for something more useful,

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:42.134 line:0%
like my Hollywood Video card.

00:11:42.134 --> 00:11:43.301 line:0%
There's a throughline here

00:11:43.301 --> 00:11:44.437
between COVID
and climate change.

00:11:44.437 --> 00:11:45.937
In both cases,
the right has decided

00:11:45.937 --> 00:11:48.840
the best course of action is
to just let disaster happen

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.443
and scare people about any
government attempt to stop it.

00:11:51.443 --> 00:11:54.012
And, while some in the GOP
advocate for vaccines,

00:11:54.012 --> 00:11:55.781 line:0%
other loud voices, like Greene,

00:11:55.781 --> 00:11:57.349 line:0%
continue to spread lies
about them.

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:59.384 line:0%
They've sunk so low,
they're basically...

00:11:59.384 --> 00:12:01.786 line:0%
-25% below sea level.

00:12:01.786 --> 00:12:03.288
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:03.288 --> 00:12:07.159
♪♪

